AB  - This study aims to investigate the role and function of costume in the ancient society by analyzing the jade decorations, 'Gui’, ‘Bi’, and ‘Hwang,' recorded in Zhouli. The method of study consisted of researching the record book Zhouli and comparing the antiquities with the images of the jades. Firstly, the jade decorations were different depending on class. The class system in Zhou dynasty was made up of 6 grades - emperor, duke, marquis, count, viscount, and baron. The jade decorations used by people in these grades were called 'Gui’, ‘Bi’, and ‘Hwang’ . Secondly, this study grasped the system of 'Gui’, ‘Bi’, and ‘Hwang.’ It identified 7 types of duties by matching the decorations on the jade to specific institutions. 'Gui’, ‘Bi’, and ‘Hwang’ played a huge role in forming and maintaining to order and system during the chaotic Zhou dynasty. In addition, it became an essential part of un- derstanding status, society, and political structure within a family power structure.
